THE RESIDUAL IS DERIVED ONCE PER (TX-DEPTH, TXB) AGAIN, AS C DOES IT: the port
re-subtracted the same `w x h` source/prediction block once per TX-TYPE TRIAL.
`residual_i32` 4,256,724 calls per 512x512 photo frame at preset 2 ->
1,307,794, against C's 1,986,776 — port/C **2.142x -> 0.658x**, -1,039 M Ir
(-2.19 %) on top of the txout chunk, byte-identical. Wall clock on a textured
photo at 512 p2: **1.016x** against the previous commit and **1.042x** against
the tree both chunks branched from; on the gradient 1.029x / 1.023x at 256 /
512 p2. The port/C instruction ratio on a photo at p2 is now **1.704**
(1.777 before this pair of commits).

