=================== C's SHAPE (cited) ===================

C derives the luma residual ONCE per (tx-depth, TXB), in
`perform_tx_partitioning`:

    product_coding_loop.c:5333    if (ctx->tx_depth) av1_intra_luma_prediction(...);
    product_coding_loop.c:5336    svt_aom_residual_kernel(input_pic->y_buffer, ...,
                                      tx_cand_bf->pred->y_buffer, ...,
                                      (int16_t*)tx_cand_bf->residual->y_buffer, ...)

and every tx-type trial inside `tx_type_search` transforms THAT buffer:

    product_coding_loop.c:4730    svt_aom_estimate_transform(pcs, ctx,
                                      &(((int16_t*)cand_bf->residual->y_buffer)[txb_origin_index]),
                                      cand_bf->residual->y_stride, ...)

`tx_type_search` has NO call-graph edge into the residual kernel at any preset
— `callcount_2026-09-04` verified that directly with `--tree=caller` (the
kernel's only C callers are `hadamard_path`, `full_loop_core`,
`perform_tx_partitioning`, `search_best_mds3_uv_mode` and the two
`pick_partition_pd0` variants). That was HEADLINE #2 of that record and item A
of `callcount_realimg_2026-09-04`'s ranked list, where the ratio was measured
to GROW with texture: 1.383x on the synthetic gradient, 2.143x on this photo,
2.184x on a CLIC glitter image — because the ratio IS the mean number of
tx-type trials per TXB.

=================== THE PORT ===================

`tx_unit_inner` opened by calling `residual::residual_i32` unconditionally, so
`txt_search`'s group loop re-derived the same subtraction once per admitted
trial. `src`, `pred`, `src_stride`, `w` and `h` are all loop-invariant across
that loop — the residual cannot depend on `tx_type` — so the fix is exactly the
shape the record named: `txt_search` fills one buffer before the loop and hands
the same slice to every trial through a new `pre_residual: Option<&[i32]>`
argument. The buffer is a third field of the per-thread `TxtScratch` that this
chunk's predecessor introduced for the two output slots, so it costs no
allocation after warmup; `None` restores the per-call derivation into
`TxScratch`'s own buffer, which is what every single-shot call site wants (MDS1,
chroma, CfL, the owned-output wrapper) and what C's `perform_dct_dct_tx` and
`full_loop_uv` likewise do.

It is applied only on the multi-candidate (`!only_dct`) path — a one-candidate
search has nothing to share a residual WITH, and leaving that path untouched is
also what keeps the preset-13 video/inter arm allocation-identical, for the
reason `txout_cshape_2026-09-05` measured the hard way.

BYTE IDENTITY IS STRUCTURAL, not empirical: the values written are the same
integer subtraction of the same two buffers, computed once instead of k times.
The two positive controls confirm no second-order effect — `fwd_txfm2d_dispatch`
4,256,724 = 4,256,724 and `optimize_b` 2,854,762 = 2,854,762, i.e. the SEARCH
BREADTH and the RDOQ work are bit-for-bit the same amount of work; only the
subtractions went away.

