The two p10 rows are the `only_dct` path, which this chunk does not touch; both
spans straddle or sit just above 1.0 and they are reported as the nulls they
are. Note the gradient gains MORE than the photo here (1.029x / 1.023x at p2
against 1.016x) while the allocator chunk gained LESS on the gradient — the two
mechanisms have opposite content dependence, which is exactly what
`callcount_realimg_2026-09-04` predicted: the allocator ratio grows with texture
(1,339x -> 9,292x) while the residual ratio is a per-TXB trial count that is
high on both (1.38x gradient, 2.14x photo) and cheaper to remove where the frame
is smaller.

